# Marketing and SEO

Implementation lives in `src/data/seo.ts`, `src/data/hire.ts` (`hirePageMeta`), and `src/lib/json-ld.ts`. Tests: `tests/unit/seo.test.ts`.

## Page meta (do not mix sources)

| Surface | Source | Index? | Notes |
| ------- | ------ | ------ | ----- |
| `/` (root layout default) | `homePageMeta` in `src/data/seo.ts` | yes | Resume-flavored title/description. No “Hire a Senior…” CTAs. |
| `/hire/` | `hirePageMeta` in `src/data/hire.ts` | yes | Document/OG title is **not** the locked H1 (`hire.headline`). Canonical `https://alytvynenko.net/hire/`. |
| `/resume/`, `/viewer/*`, `/privacy-policy/`, `/cookie-policy/` | page-local `metadata` | **noindex**, follow | Viewer + legal + resume iframe stay out of the index. |

Open Graph / Twitter on home and `/hire/` use `summary_large_image` and the profile WebP. Home OG type is `profile`; `/hire/` is `website`.

When you change a public title or description, update the matching `*Meta` object and `tests/unit/seo.test.ts` in the same PR.

## Structured data (JSON-LD)

`src/app/layout.tsx` injects **one** node: `personJsonLd` from `src/lib/json-ld.ts`.

The public `Person` includes name, jobTitle, url, image, address (Częstochowa, PL), `sameAs`, `knowsAbout`, and `hasCredential` (earned certs only — rows in `certificates.ts` that have a `link`).

**Do not reintroduce** (tests fail if these appear):

- `email`, `worksFor`, `seeks`, or `JobPosting`
- `ProfessionalService` / `OfferCatalog` (acquisition schema is off while the competitive hold stands)
- Employer name Geniusee on the schema
- Extra JSON-LD on `/hire/` — that page is HTML + Open Graph only

`hasCredential` is derived from `certificates.filter((cert) => Boolean(cert.link))`. Adding an earned cert with a verification URL updates schema automatically.

## Sitemap and robots

- `public/sitemap.xml` lists `/`, `/hire/`, `/resume/`, and the two policy pages. Bump `lastmod` when the URL’s public content changes.
- Policy and resume routes stay in the sitemap but send `robots: noindex`.
- `/hire/` is in the sitemap (`priority` 0.8) even though primary nav does not link it.

## Personal brand constraints

- Home hero and About stay resume-led (AWS-first career proof).
- `/hire/` is the conversion surface: AWS-first packages, case-study outcomes (not guaranteed %), proof teasers to `/#experience`.
- Academic/labs (GCP diploma org) stays on Education only — not home meta, not `/hire`.
- Authenticity: claims on `/hire/` must already appear on Experience or profile highlights (unit tests check 50% / 70% / Luxoft / TFE timing).
